/-!
# The special fibre of a regular model is numerically trivial

Let `R` be a local ring of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `π`, for instance a discrete valuation ring with a uniformizer, and let `X` be a
regular Noetherian integral scheme, flat over `R`, all of whose points have codimension at most
two, such as a regular model of a curve over `R`. The special fibre is the effective Cartier
divisor `X_s = Σᵢ mᵢ Cᵢ`, where the `Cᵢ` are its irreducible components with their reduced
structures and `mᵢ` their multiplicities
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ker_specialFiberι_eq_prod_vanishingIdeal`), and its ideal sheaf is
trivial, generated by the global function `π`
(`TauCeti.mk_toInvertibleSheaf_ker_specialFiberι`). Hence the divisor `Σᵢ mᵢ Cᵢ` is linearly
equivalent to zero: in the Picard group of `X`,

`∏ᵢ [𝒪_X(Cᵢ)] ^ mᵢ = 1`.

Taking degrees on a proper integral curve `C` over a field `k` mapping to `X` gives the
fundamental relation between the intersection numbers `(Cᵢ · C) = deg_k 𝒪_X(Cᵢ)|_C` of
`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber`:

`Σᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · C) = 0`.

For `C` one of the components `Cⱼ`, this computes the self-intersection of `Cⱼ` from its
intersections with the other components,

`mⱼ (Cⱼ · Cⱼ) = -Σ_{i ≠ j} mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cⱼ)`.

Since distinct prime divisors on a regular surface meet properly, their intersection numbers are
nonnegative, and hence the self-intersection of every component is nonpositive,
`(Cⱼ · Cⱼ) ≤ 0`. These are the relations `Σᵢ aⱼᵢ mᵢ = 0` and the sign conditions satisfied by the
intersection matrix `aⱼᵢ = (Cᵢ · Cⱼ)` of the special fibre: the hypotheses from which
`Matrix.dotProduct_mulVec_nonpos_of_mulVec_eq_zero` deduces that the intersection form is negative
semidefinite, once the matrix is known to be symmetric.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.prod_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf_vanishingIdeal_pow_eq_one`: the
  divisor `Σᵢ mᵢ Cᵢ` of the special fibre is linearly equivalent to zero.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.sum_specialFiberMultiplicity_mul_intersectionNumber_eq_zero`:
  `Σᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · C) = 0` for every proper integral curve `C` over a field mapping to `X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultiplicity_mul_intersectionNumber_self`: the
  self-intersection formula `mⱼ (Cⱼ · Cⱼ) = -Σ_{i ≠ j} mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cⱼ)`.
* `LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf_nonneg_of_ne`:
  distinct prime divisors on a regular surface have nonnegative intersection number.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.intersectionNumber_self_nonpos`: `(Cⱼ · Cⱼ) ≤ 0`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C9U), where the
  intersection numbers of the components of the special fibre of a regular model satisfy
  `Σᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cⱼ) = 0`.
* Q. Liu, *Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Curves*, Section 9.1, on the intersection of the
  special fibre with vertical divisors on a regular fibred surface.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing Order
open TauCeti TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData (vanishingIdeal
  isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular
  isEffectiveCartier_comap_subschemeι_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular)

universe u

namespace TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass

/-- **Distinct prime divisors on a regular surface meet nonnegatively.** On a regular scheme `X`
all of whose points have codimension at most two, let `η ≠ η'` be codimension-one points, and
suppose that the closure `C` of `η`, with its reduced structure, is a proper curve over a field `k`
with finite-dimensional `H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)` and `H¹(C, 𝒪_C)`. Then the intersection number of the prime
divisor `C'`, the closure of `η'`, with `C` is nonnegative: `(C' · C) = dim_k Γ(C' ∩ C) ≥ 0`. -/
theorem intersectionNumber_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf_nonneg_of_ne (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X] (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    {η η' : CodimensionOnePoint X} (hne : η ≠ η')
    [(vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [IsProper ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [RelativeDimensionLE 1
      ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0)]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1)] :
    0 ≤ intersectionNumber k (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι
      (mk (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular
        hX η'.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ := by
  rw [intersectionNumber_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf k _ _
    (isEffectiveCartier_comap_subschemeι_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX hne)
    default]
  exact Nat.cast_nonneg _

end TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Ring.DimensionLEOne R]
  {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [Flat toBase] [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X]

/-- **The special fibre is linearly equivalent to zero.** Let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral
scheme, flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `π`, with all points of codimension at most two and generic point away from the
closed point. Then the divisor `Σᵢ mᵢ Cᵢ` of the components `Cᵢ` of the special fibre, with their
multiplicities `mᵢ`, is linearly equivalent to zero: `∏ᵢ [𝒪_X(Cᵢ)] ^ mᵢ = 1` in the Picard group
of `X`. -/
theorem prod_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf_vanishingIdeal_pow_eq_one
    (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2) (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) {π : R}
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π) :
    ∏ η ∈ (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (fun h ↦ hη (PrimeSpectrum.ext (le_antisymm
          (le_maximalIdeal (toBase (genericPoint X)).isPrime.ne_top) (h.le.trans bot_le))))
        hη).toFinset,
      (LineBundleClass.mk (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular
        hX η.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ ^ toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π η = 1 := by
  have hC (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) :=
    isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX η.2
  -- The class of an effective Cartier divisor depends only on its ideal sheaf.
  have hmk {I J : X.IdealSheafData} (hI : I.IsEffectiveCartier) (hJ : J.IsEffectiveCartier)
      (e : I = J) :
      LineBundleClass.mk hI.toInvertibleSheaf = LineBundleClass.mk hJ.toInvertibleSheaf := by
    subst e
    rfl
  -- The ideal sheaf `𝒪_X(-X_s) = ∏ᵢ 𝒪_X(-Cᵢ) ^ mᵢ` has trivial class.
  have h := mk_toInvertibleSheaf_ker_specialFiberι toBase hπ hreg
    (isEffectiveCartier_ker_specialFiberι toBase hπ hreg)
  rw [hmk _ (isEffectiveCartier_prod fun η _ ↦ isEffectiveCartier_pow (hC η) _)
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_eq_prod_vanishingIdeal hX hη hπ),
    LineBundleClass.mk_toInvertibleSheaf_prod _ fun η ↦ isEffectiveCartier_pow (hC η) _,
    Finset.prod_congr rfl fun η _ ↦ LineBundleClass.mk_toInvertibleSheaf_pow (hC η) _] at h
  simp only [inv_pow, Finset.prod_inv_distrib, h, inv_one]

section IntersectionNumber

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- **The special fibre is numerically trivial.** Let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral scheme,
flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `π`, with all points of codimension at most two and generic point away from the
closed point. Let `C` be a proper integral curve over a field `k`, with finite-dimensional
`H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)` and `H¹(C, 𝒪_C)`, mapping to `X` by `ι`. Then the components `Cᵢ` of the special
fibre, with their multiplicities `mᵢ`, satisfy `Σᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · C) = 0`. -/
theorem sum_specialFiberMultiplicity_mul_intersectionNumber_eq_zero
    {C : Scheme.{u}} [C.Over (Spec (.of k))] [IsIntegral C] [IsProper (C ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [RelativeDimensionLE 1 (C ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial C).obj 0)]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial C).obj 1)] (ι : C ⟶ X)
    (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2) (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) {π : R}
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π) :
    ∑ η ∈ (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (fun h ↦ hη (PrimeSpectrum.ext (le_antisymm
          (le_maximalIdeal (toBase (genericPoint X)).isPrime.ne_top) (h.le.trans bot_le))))
        hη).toFinset,
      (toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π η : ℤ) * LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber k ι
        (LineBundleClass.mk (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular
          hX η.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ = 0 := by
  have h := congrArg (LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber k ι)
    (toBase.prod_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf_vanishingIdeal_pow_eq_one hX hη hπ hreg)
  rwa [LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_prod_of_isIntegral,
    LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_one, Finset.sum_congr rfl fun η _ ↦
      LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_pow_of_isIntegral k ι _ _] at h

open scoped Classical in
/-- **The self-intersection of a component of the special fibre.** Let `X` be a regular Noetherian
integral scheme, flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is
generated by a nonzerodivisor `π`, with all points of codimension at most two and generic point
away from the closed point. Let `Cⱼ` be a component of the special fibre, with its reduced
structure, which is a proper curve over a field `k` with finite-dimensional `H⁰` and `H¹` of its
structure sheaf. Then its self-intersection is determined by its intersections with the other
components `Cᵢ`: `mⱼ (Cⱼ · Cⱼ) = -Σ_{i ≠ j} mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cⱼ)`. -/
theorem specialFiberMultiplicity_mul_intersectionNumber_self (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) {π : R}
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π)
    {j : CodimensionOnePoint X} (hj : toBase j = closedPoint R)
    [(vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [IsProper ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [RelativeDimensionLE 1
      ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0)]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1)] :
    (toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j : ℤ) * LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber k
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι
        (LineBundleClass.mk (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular
          hX j.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ =
      -∑ η ∈ ((toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (fun h ↦ hη (PrimeSpectrum.ext (le_antisymm
            (le_maximalIdeal (toBase (genericPoint X)).isPrime.ne_top) (h.le.trans bot_le))))
          hη).toFinset).erase j,
        (toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π η : ℤ) * LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber k
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι
          (LineBundleClass.mk (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular
            hX η.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ := by
  have h := toBase.sum_specialFiberMultiplicity_mul_intersectionNumber_eq_zero k
    (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι hX hη hπ hreg
  rw [← Finset.add_sum_erase _ _ (by simpa using hj)] at h
  exact eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left h

/-- **The self-intersection of a component of the special fibre is nonpositive.** Let `X` be a
regular Noetherian integral scheme, flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one whose
maximal ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor `π`, with all points of codimension at most two and
generic point away from the closed point. Let `Cⱼ` be a component of the special fibre, with its
reduced structure, which is a proper curve over a field `k` with finite-dimensional `H⁰` and `H¹`
of its structure sheaf. Then `(Cⱼ · Cⱼ) ≤ 0`. -/
theorem intersectionNumber_self_nonpos (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) {π : R}
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π)
    {j : CodimensionOnePoint X} (hj : toBase j = closedPoint R)
    [(vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [IsProper ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [RelativeDimensionLE 1
      ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0)]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1)] :
    LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber k
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(j : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι
        (LineBundleClass.mk (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular
          hX j.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ ≤ 0 := by
  -- If `R` were a field, its generic point would map to the closed point.
  have hR : maximalIdeal R ≠ ⊥ := fun h ↦ hη (PrimeSpectrum.ext (le_antisymm
    (le_maximalIdeal (toBase (genericPoint X)).isPrime.ne_top) (h.le.trans bot_le)))
  have hπ0 : π ≠ 0 := fun h ↦ hR (by rw [hπ, h, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot])
  have hm := toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_pos hη (hπ ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self π) hπ0 j hj
  refine nonpos_of_mul_nonpos_right ?_ (Nat.cast_pos.mpr hm)
  rw [toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_mul_intersectionNumber_self k hX hη hπ hreg hj, neg_nonpos]
  -- Every other component meets `Cⱼ` nonnegatively.
  classical
  exact Finset.sum_nonneg fun η hη' ↦ mul_nonneg (Nat.cast_nonneg _)
    (LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf_nonneg_of_ne k hX
      (Finset.ne_of_mem_erase hη').symm)

end IntersectionNumber

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom
